  "summary": "Recent preprints examine how disorder and scattering shape Hall plateaus, orbital Hall response, and anisotropic magnetotransport in topological materials.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how disorder and scattering modify transport in topological and orbital-active band structures. In twisted bilayer MoTe2, layer-dependent disorder is reported to shape integer and fractional Hall plateau widths and transitions in Chern insulators. For an sp3 centrosymmetric square tight-binding lattice, Kubo-Bastin Chebyshev calculations probe the robustness and tunability of orbital Hall transport under disorder, linked to a quadrupole origin. In multi-Weyl semimetals, a generalized semiclassical Boltzmann treatment beyond the constant relaxation-time approximation highlights orbital moment and intervalley scattering in anisotropic magnetotransport, parameterized by monopole charge N. What is new across these preprints is the explicit treatment of disorder or scattering beyond idealized descriptions, applied to three distinct platforms.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
